# Cloudflare Pages response headers for businessvideosolutions.net.
#
# Copied into out/ by `next build` and read from the build output root.
#
# Syntax: a path pattern on its own line, then each header indented by two
# spaces as `Name: value`. Rules are additive — a request matching several
# patterns receives the headers from all of them. Limits: 100 rules, and 2,000
# characters per line.
#
# Comments are kept at column 0 throughout. Cloudflare only documents
# top-level `#` comments, and an indented one risks being parsed as a header
# name, so nothing inside a rule block is ever a comment.
#
# ─── What each header on /* is for ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   X-Frame-Options            clickjacking; nothing needs to frame this site
#   X-Content-Type-Options     stop MIME sniffing turning an upload into script
#   Referrer-Policy            full referrer same-origin, origin-only cross-site
#   Permissions-Policy         deny hardware APIs the site never uses. `payment`
#                              is deliberately left enabled so the booking
#                              widget's payment step can request it
#   Strict-Transport-Security  force HTTPS for two years. Do NOT submit to
#                              hstspreload.org until the custom domain has been
#                              serving HTTPS correctly for a while — see DEPLOY.md
#
# ─── Content-Security-Policy ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Tuned for: Next.js static export + the GoHighLevel booking iframe + video.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE EDITING THE POLICY:
# CSP is per-document. This governs OUR page only. The booking widget at
# get.businessvideosolutions.net is a separate document in a nested browsing
# context and serves no CSP of its own, so everything IT loads
# (stcdn/backend/images.leadconnectorhq.com, cdn.filesafe.space,
# storage.googleapis.com, fonts.gstatic.com, js.authorize.net, …) is governed
# by the widget's context, NOT by this header. Those hosts deliberately do not
# appear below; listing them would imply a control we do not have.
#
# What the policy genuinely has to permit for booking to work:
#
#   script-src   https://link.msgsndr.com — GHL's parent-side embed script,
#                which drives iframe auto-resizing. Verified live: it loads no
#                further external hosts of its own.
#   frame-src    the widget origin, plus the wider *.leadconnectorhq.com and
#                *.msgsndr.com families. The wildcards are NOT laziness: if the
#                widget ever navigates ITSELF to another GHL host mid-flow,
#                that navigation IS checked against our frame-src, and a miss
#                would break booking with only a console error to show for it.
#   connect-src  the LeadConnector backends, as a hedge in case a future
#                form_embed.js starts pinging them from the parent page.
#
# script-src 'unsafe-inline' is unavoidable: a Next.js static export inlines
# its hydration bootstrap and there is no server to mint a per-request nonce.
#
# If analytics or a font CDN is added later, extend the specific directive
# rather than loosening the policy wholesale. If booking ever breaks after a
# GHL change, the browser console names the blocked host — add it, do not
# delete the policy.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(self), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: off
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; form-action 'self' https://get.businessvideosolutions.net; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://link.msgsndr.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; font-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self' https:; connect-src 'self' https://backend.leadconnectorhq.com https://services.leadconnectorhq.com; frame-src 'self' https://get.businessvideosolutions.net https://*.leadconnectorhq.com https://*.msgsndr.com https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Next.js content-hashes everything under /_next/static, so it is safe to cache
# forever. Biggest repeat-visit win available.

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Assets in public/ are not content-hashed: a day in the browser, a week at the
# edge, revalidating in the background.

/*.woff2
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, s-maxage=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, s-maxage=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, s-maxage=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, s-maxage=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, s-maxage=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/*.mp4
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, s-maxage=604800

# HTML must revalidate so a content edit goes live on the next deploy.

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
